Description
This program implements a binary search tree from scratch using a node struct and a BinarySearchTree class. It includes insertion, searching, removal, inorder, preorder, and postorder traversals, as well as calculating the tree's height. The program inserts 11 different integers, searches for both an existing and a nonexistent value, and demonstrates all three removal cases: removing a leaf node, a node with one child, and a node with two children. After each removal, inorder traversal confirms that the values remain sorted and the BST structure is maintained.

Requirements
- C++17 compiler
- No additional libraries required.

Expected Output
The program displays all three traversal orders, the tree height, search results, and inorder traversal after each removal.
